<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">
  <PropertyGroup>
    <!-- NuGet packaging metadata -->
    <Description>Composition base for Platform.SharedKernel microservices: AddServiceDefaults (OpenTelemetry traces, metrics, and logs with ambient CorrelationId/TenantId log enrichment, plus the startup readiness gate), liveness and readiness endpoint mapping, StartupGate, the With*Telemetry family for every SharedKernel domain, HealthCheckNames/HealthCheckTags, and opt-in rate limiting. References no other SharedKernel package. Dependency-specific readiness checks, mutual TLS, Azure Key Vault, and localization live in the SharedKernel.ServiceDefaults.* integration packages, so a service restores only the integrations it actually uses.</Description>
    <PackageTags>shared-kernel;service-defaults;opentelemetry;health-checks;kubernetes;observability</PackageTags>
    <!--
      NU5104: a stable package release must not depend on a prerelease package. This package
      depends on OpenTelemetry.Instrumentation.EntityFrameworkCore, which as of this writing has
      never shipped a stable (non-beta) release upstream — there is no stable version to pin to.
      Suppressed at pack time only; re-evaluate and remove this suppression once OpenTelemetry
      ships a stable EFCore instrumentation release.
    -->
    <NoWarn>$(NoWarn);NU5104</NoWarn>
    <TreatWarningsAsErrors>true</TreatWarningsAsErrors>
    <!-- Per-project: the SDK assigns false before the Directory.Build.targets default is evaluated. -->
    <GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>
  </PropertyGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <FrameworkReference Include="Microsoft.AspNetCore.App" />
  </ItemGroup>
  <!--
    WO-084: this package deliberately has NO ProjectReference. Before the split it carried fourteen,
    and a project referencing it alone restored 25 SharedKernel projects and 73 NuGet packages —
    MassTransit, Azure Service Bus, Microsoft.Identity.Web, EF Core, Temporalio, Quartz, and
    StackExchange.Redis among them. Two of the fourteen (SharedKernel.Primitives and
    SharedKernel.Messaging.MassTransit) were used by no source file at all.

    Every integration that needs another SharedKernel package lives in its own
    SharedKernel.ServiceDefaults.* package. Adding a ProjectReference here reintroduces the problem
    for every service on the platform, and is locked out by two tests in
    SharedKernel.ServiceDefaults.Tests: a type-level dependency check, and a project-file check that
    catches an unused reference the type-level check cannot see.

    The With*Telemetry extensions need no reference: each wires its domain's ActivitySource and
    Meter by string name.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="OpenTelemetry.Extensions.Hosting" />
    <PackageReference Include="OpenTelemetry.Instrumentation.AspNetCore" />
    <PackageReference Include="OpenTelemetry.Instrumentation.Http" />
    <!-- Depends on OpenTelemetry and Microsoft.Extensions only — NOT on EF Core; it observes EF Core's DiagnosticSource. -->
    <PackageReference Include="OpenTelemetry.Instrumentation.EntityFrameworkCore" />
    <PackageReference Include="OpenTelemetry.Instrumentation.Runtime" />
    <PackageReference Include="OpenTelemetry.Exporter.OpenTelemetryProtocol" />
    <!--
      Activated by WithCommunicationTelemetry() only, never by AddSharedKernelTelemetry(). Depends on
      OpenTelemetry alone. Version-aligned with SharedKernel.Communication.Grpc's pin so a service
      using both never resolves two different beta builds. Polly's "Polly" Meter needs no reference:
      it is reached by name (AddMeter("Polly")), and Polly creates no ActivitySource.
    -->
    <PackageReference Include="OpenTelemetry.Instrumentation.GrpcNetClient" />
    <!--
      Microsoft.Extensions.Diagnostics.HealthChecks and Microsoft.Extensions.Hosting ship in the
      Microsoft.AspNetCore.App shared framework (see FrameworkReference above); an explicit reference
      is flagged redundant by NU1510 and fails the build under TreatWarningsAsErrors.
    -->
  </ItemGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="SharedKernel.ServiceDefaults.Tests" />
  </ItemGroup>
</Project>
